course: dictionary
lesson: 6150
title: Big numbers and the word million
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A million is the number 1,000,000, which is a thousand thousands. It has six zeros. In place value, the digits in a million sit in the millions column, then the hundred thousands, ten thousands and thousands columns.
explain: Writers also use million when they do not mean an exact number. «Each year more than a million wildebeest follow the rain» means a huge crowd. The words «more than» show the count is rough, not exact.
explain: Look for the words that go with million. «Millions of» means a very large number, not an exact one. «One in a million» means very rare or special. «A millionaire» is someone who has a million pounds, dollars or more.
fact: A million is 1,000,000, which is a thousand thousands.
fact: One million has six zeros.
fact: «Millions of» means a very large number, not an exact one.
fact: «One in a million» means very rare or special.
fact: «About 476 million Indigenous people live today» shows that a million can be used for a huge number of people, and «about» tells you it is an estimate.
exercise: «Each year more than a million wildebeest follow the rain.» How many is one million? | 10 | *1,000,000 | 1,000 | 100,000
exercise: What does «one in a million» mean? | *Very rare or special | Very common | Half a million | Exactly one million
exercise: «The narwhal's tusk has millions of tiny nerve channels.» Does millions mean an exact number? | *No, it means a very large number, not an exact one | No, it means zero | Yes, exactly six | Yes, exactly two million
test: How many zeros are in one million? | Four | Three | *Six | Nine
test: Which number is a thousand thousands? | Ten thousand | A hundred | A thousand | *A million
exam: Which number is two million written in figures? | 20,000 | *2,000,000 | 2,000 | 200,000
